## Epic 1: HubSpot Integration (End-to-End)
**Owner:** BD · **Weeks 1-2** · **Priority: 🔴 Critical**

The entire product hinges on this. A customer connects HubSpot, and from that moment, everything should just work — team members sync, deal data flows, celebrations fire, KPIs show real numbers.

**Stories:**

- **Fix OAuth flow** — The current OAuth has three known bugs (empty credentials on callback, user-org membership mismatch on authorize, lingering quotes-scope error). OAuth must work cleanly: admin clicks Connect → redirects to HubSpot → comes back with valid tokens stored.

- **Schema discovery & caching** — After connecting, fetch the customer's HubSpot schema (deal properties, pipelines, stages, owners) and cache it. The admin UI needs this to render dynamic dropdowns so customers map their own CRM fields without typing raw property names.

- **Owner sync** — Automatically pull HubSpot owners into team_members with their hubspot_owner_id in external_ids. This is how celebrations resolve "who closed the deal" → show their photo.

- **Webhook signature verification** — Verify HubSpot's v3 signature header before processing any webhook. Reject replays older than 5 minutes.

- **Enrich-on-event** — HubSpot webhooks only send object IDs. On each webhook, fetch the full deal object (properties + associated company) from HubSpot before evaluating trigger conditions. This is how we get deal name, amount, company name, etc.

- **Token refresh** — Handle expired access tokens gracefully everywhere (schema fetch, owner sync, webhook enrichment, KPI queries). Refresh and retry once; surface errors to admin if refresh fails.

**Done when:** An admin connects HubSpot, their team members appear automatically, and changing a deal stage in HubSpot fires a celebration on the TV display with the correct deal name, amount, company, and team member photo.

