## Epic 7: TV Display Redesign
**Owner:** MF · **Weeks 2-5** · **Priority: 🔴 Critical**

The TV display is the product. It needs to go from "functional prototype" to "makes people stop and stare." Design in Figma first, then build.

**Stories:**

- **Figma: Dashboard idle state (3 themes)** — 1920×1080 frames for dark, light, and vibrant themes. New KPI cards with visual depth, leaderboard with prominent photos, recent wins feed, content carousel, running counter, header. Define color tokens, typography scale, and spacing system.

- **Figma: Celebration overlay** — Full-screen takeover with dramatic entrance. Three particle visual styles (confetti, fireworks, champagne). GIF integration in 4 positions. Staggered content entrance animations. Amount count-up. Component library frame with all tokens and specs.

- **Build dashboard layout from Figma** — Complete layout rebuild with new grid, cards, themes. CSS custom properties for all 3 themes. Ambient animations (subtle glow shifts, transitions, breathing effects) that make the screen feel alive without being distracting.

- **Build running counter** — Persistent number that animates up when celebrations fire. Smooth count-up, +delta flyout, milestone flash effects (e.g., golden burst when crossing $500K). Idle breathing animation.

- **Build celebration overlay** — Three particle systems (confetti with 5 shapes, fireworks with burst patterns, champagne with rising bubbles). GIF integration in 4 positions. Staggered content entrance. Amount count-up and slot-machine animation options. Preload GIFs on template fetch.

- **Ambient dashboard animations** — Subtle idle motion: card border glow shifts, leaderboard rank slide transitions, feed crossfade, connection status pulse, optional background grain. All CSS-only, GPU-friendly. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

**Done when:** The TV display looks like it was designed by a product design team, not generated by a dev. All 3 themes work. Celebrations are visually dramatic. The screen never feels frozen during idle.

